# A confrontation holds the whole party: only the members somebody confronts may do anything.
#
# Members of the party stand where they were left, so one of them can be confronted alone. Until
# that is settled nobody else acts: the view goes to the confronted member by itself, the others'
# tokens cannot be played (their label says they wait), until the confrontation is settled.
#
# The protagonist follows the track to the Test Rock and the companion stays in the Test Field.
# The companion is then played, and the brewer is made an enemy at the rock (`hostile`).
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --fill-party --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Field" --period dawn --observe-only "Field–Rock Track"

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

strategy succeed
goal follow_path
advance 12 180
click observe "Field–Rock Track"
choose childhood_memory
advance 12 180
click think "Field–Rock Track"
choose ripelore
advance 12 180
click act 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180
expect Moved to: Test Rock
click continue
advance 12 180

# The companion, left in the field, is played: nobody is confronted, so they answer.
inspect party
click member Brindletail
wait
expect [BRINDLETAIL]

# An enemy at the rock, where only the protagonist stands. The view goes to the one confronted.
hostile brewer Test Rock
wait
expect [KENRYC GREYGATE]
expect-state where area=Test Rock
expect-state where confronted=Enemy:brewer exit=RUNAWAY

# The companion cannot be played while it lasts, and says why.
click member Brindletail
wait
expect [KENRYC GREYGATE]
point member Brindletail
wait
expect-state pointer-label ground=grey text=Brindletail · waits: confrontation

# The confronted member is not held: the one standing in the way can be looked at.
expect-state symbols click observe hostile in Test Rock
expect-no-state symbols click observe hostile in Test Rock x1 (disabled)
quit
